of Mr. Kaplan, you know,

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.530
we've developed this PRK Fellows program

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:43.050
at the Jackson School for
Global Affairs at Yale,

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.150
which has really, helped bring

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.210
the special operations
community into contact

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.800
with the outstanding resources

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.770
that we have here on the Yale campus

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.900
and its teaching and research mission.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.030
But I actually think
it's just as beneficial,

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.780
if not more for the students
who are not in that community.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.370
And so to be able to learn

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.580
and interact with all of you
on the daily basis, you know,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.500
the work that Mike and
his colleagues have done

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.360
in putting this conference together,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.920
it's inspirational for our students.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.590
It helps enhance the
public service mission

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.570
of what we're trying to do at Yale.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.340
And it's been central to this effort

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.790
to build this Jackson School
of Global Affairs at Yale.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.330
So it's the first new
school that Yale has created

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.060
in nearly 50 years since
our business school,

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.380
and reflects a real commitment
to putting challenges

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.350
and diplomacy and international
security, you know,

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.050
front and center at the
mission of the university

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:38.550
in really exciting ways.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:39.600
I'm Ted Wittenstein.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.660
I teach at the Jackson
School and at the law school,

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.750
and I oversee our international
security studies program

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.280
here at the Jackson School,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.970
which includes what we now
call the Schmidt program

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.560
on artificial intelligence,

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.080
emerging technologies
